            {/* 11. Client Responsibilities */}
            <section id="client-responsibilities" className="space-y-4">
              <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold text-white">11. Client Responsibilities During Remote Sessions</h2>
              <div className="text-[14px] leading-[1.9] text-white/55 font-light space-y-4">
                <p>To ensure a smooth, efficient, and effective Remote Session, and to minimize risks to your system and data, you agree to fulfill the following responsibilities, each of which is a material condition of Impulse's willingness to provide Services:</p>
                <ul className="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 marker:text-white/35">
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Prepare your system:</strong> Before the scheduled session, you must download, install, and test the designated remote desktop software. Your system must meet the minimum requirements: Windows 10 version 1903 or later, or Windows 11, 64-bit architecture, a stable internet connection with at least 10 Mbps download speed and 5 Mbps upload speed, and sufficient disk space for any temporary files or tools used during the session.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Back up your data:</strong> You are solely and entirely responsible for creating a complete, verified backup of all important data, files, documents, applications, settings, and system images before any Remote Session. Impulse strongly recommends creating a full system image backup and a separate file-level backup before booking any Service, particularly overclocking and BIOS modification services. Impulse shall have no liability for any data loss, data corruption, or failure to restore data, regardless of the cause.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Provide necessary access:</strong> You must provide the remote desktop connection credentials (session ID and password) to the technician at the scheduled session time. Where required for the Service, you must also provide administrator account credentials for your Windows user account. You may change your account password immediately after the session for security purposes.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Be present and available:</strong> You must be physically present at your Client Device and available for communication during the entire Remote Session, either through Discord voice chat, text chat, or other communication method as arranged. Your presence is required to answer the technician's questions, provide feedback on changes, authorize specific modifications, and perform any actions that require physical access to the machine.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Secure sensitive information:</strong> Before the session begins, you must close, minimize, or otherwise secure any applications, windows, tabs, or files that display sensitive, private, confidential, or personal information, including but not limited to banking applications, password managers, personal documents, private messages, email clients, and any other applications containing information you do not wish the technician to see.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Ensure stable power and connectivity:</strong> If using a laptop, notebook, or other battery-powered device, ensure it is connected to a reliable power source throughout the entire session. Do not rely on battery power, as system modifications and stress testing can significantly increase power consumption and may cause unexpected shutdowns if battery power is depleted.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Provide accurate and complete information:</strong> You must provide accurate, complete, and truthful information about your system configuration, hardware specifications, software environment, usage patterns, performance goals, any known issues or problems, and any previous modifications or optimizations that have been applied to your system.</li>
                  <li><strong className="text-white/60">Test and verify results:</strong> After the session is complete, you should thoroughly test your system to verify that the optimizations meet your expectations and do not cause any unacceptable side effects. You should report any issues, concerns, or adverse effects to Impulse within forty-eight (48) hours of session completion so that Impulse can evaluate and address them.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Your failure to fulfill any of the responsibilities set forth in this Section 11 may result in suboptimal results, incomplete Services, the inability to perform certain optimizations, increased risk to your system, or the inability to complete the Service. Impulse shall not be liable for any consequences arising from your failure to fulfill these responsibilities.</p>
              </div>
            </section>

